ble"},{"text":" values, kept in an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrderedSet"},{"text":" whose element ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":" is vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":": the vertices listed first, then new members by first appearance, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assigns them. A hyperedge is a set of vertices of any size, the empty set included; repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedges are kept, each at its own position ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"text":", and a member listed twice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is stored once. Members are stored in vertex-index order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage is compressed sparse rows: the members of every hyperedge in one array, and for every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex its incidence numbers and, beside them, its hyperedge positions, in rows of shared","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pools. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)"},{"text":" are stored ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArraySlice<Int>"},{"text":" rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read without hashing, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hypergraph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" algorithms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hash none.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragr